# This CITATION.cff file was generated with the intention of making
# citation of the SPATBench benchmark archive straightforward.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SPATBench in your work, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "SPATBench: Methodological Choices Can Outweigh Algorithmic Choices in Transcriptomic Immunotherapy Prediction Benchmarking at Current Sample Sizes"
authors:
  - family-names: Huang
    given-names: Zhixian
    affiliation: "Putian University, Putian, Fujian, China"
keywords:
  - cancer immunotherapy
  - biomarker benchmarking
  - response definition
  - feature selection
  - endpoint circularity
  - transcriptomics
  - machine learning
  - immune checkpoint inhibitors
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/huangzhixian324-dev/spa-bench"
version: v34-submission
date-released: "2026-09-16"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22746254
abstract: "SPATBench is an open-source, Docker-reproducible benchmark framework that isolates three benchmarking design choices (response definition, feature selection, and endpoint circularity) across six prediction methods and five immunotherapy-treated cohorts (196 patients; melanoma, NSCLC, bladder). It includes the full analysis pipeline, the CDS circularity-detection package (v1.2.1), machine-readable results, figures, and manuscript source."
